Copyright: work module for the Elgindi finite-time singularity project.

# The coefficient recursion for `L^i (sin(2θ))`, `L = sin(2θ) ∂_θ`

The angular operator `L = D_θ = sin(2θ) ∂_θ` acts on functions of `θ` alone as
`Work.Spaces.Lop u θ = sin(2θ) u'(θ)`.  Since `sin(2θ)' = 2 cos(2θ)`, the operator maps the
ideal generated by `s(θ) = sin(2θ)` into itself:

`L (s · h) = s · (2 cos(2θ) · h + s · h')`.

Hence every iterate of `s` is divisible by `s`:

`L^i (s) = s · hfun i`,

where the coefficient functions `hfun i` are given by the recursion of this file:

* `hfun 0 = 1`;
* `hfun (i+1) = fun θ => 2 cos(2θ) · hfun i θ + sin(2θ) · deriv (hfun i) θ`.

`hfun` is used by `Work.FTS.EllipticEst.Lop_iter_sin_bound`, whose statement is that the
functions `L^i (s)`, `i ≤ K`, are all `O(s)` on `Iθ = [0, π/2]`; equivalently that the
finitely many coefficients `hfun i`, `i ≤ K`, are bounded on the compact `Iθ`.
-/
import Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.Deriv.Basic
import Mathlib.Analysis.Complex.Trigonometric
import Submission.Work.FTS.EllipticEst.ThetaPoincareDefs

-- v435-port: begin
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.instanceSearchTypes false
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false
-- v435-port: end

noncomputable section

open scoped Real Topology

namespace Work.FTS.EllipticEst

set_option autoImplicit false

/-- The coefficient recursion attached to `L = sin(2θ) ∂_θ` and the special function
`sin(2θ)`:  `hfun 0 = 1` and
`hfun (i+1) θ = 2 cos(2θ) hfun i θ + sin(2θ) · deriv (hfun i) θ`, so that (see
`LopIter_sin_factor`) one has `L^i (sin(2θ)) = fun θ => sin(2θ) · hfun i θ`. -/
noncomputable def hfun : ℕ → ℝ → ℝ
  | 0 => fun _ => 1
  | (n + 1) => fun θ => 2 * Real.cos (2 * θ) * hfun n θ
      + Real.sin (2 * θ) * deriv (hfun n) θ

@[simp] theorem hfun_zero : hfun 0 = fun _ : ℝ => 1 := rfl

@[simp] theorem hfun_succ (n : ℕ) :
    hfun (n + 1) = fun θ => 2 * Real.cos (2 * θ) * hfun n θ
      + Real.sin (2 * θ) * deriv (hfun n) θ := rfl

end Work.FTS.EllipticEst
